# Copilot Instructions

## Tool Priority
1. FIRST: `ccc search "semantic description"` — zero token cost, finds exact file:line
2. SECOND: read graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md for architecture/community relationships
3. LAST RESORT: read specific file:line ranges (only after steps 1-2 narrow the target)
Never read full files. Never grep the raw codebase without searching first.

## Self-Audit Protocol
Before reporting work, verify:
- [ ] No full files read without prior ccc search
- [ ] No new files created unless strictly necessary
- [ ] No code written beyond what was asked
- [ ] Report uses STATUS / COMPLETED / BLOCKED / FILES_CHANGED / TESTS / NEXT_RECOMMENDED / CONFIDENCE

## Project
UAV Six Degrees of Freedom (6DOF) flight controller based on FreeRTOS with ground station integration.

## Architecture
- **Kernel**: FreeRTOS real-time operating system
- **Target**: STM32 microcontroller (inferred from BSP)
- **Main Components**:
  - FreeRTOS kernel and task scheduler
  - Board support package (BSP)
  - Sensor APIs (IMU, GPS)
  - Ground station communication
  - User application tasks

See docs/architecture.md for detailed structure.

## Style
- C/C++ code for embedded systems
- FreeRTOS task-based architecture
- Follow existing code conventions in API/, USER/, and TASK/ directories
